new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b380aa7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/fixtures/reports/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Report importer incident archive
+
+The raw attachments under each format come from client workflows. Each .checks.json is a capture of fields consumed by the UI, or the physical source line shown by the error inspector. Keys beginning with / are JSON Pointers. Other output fields still follow the existing importer. Archive tests read the actual files through the public entry point. Keep the old unit tests, inputs, and captured expectations intact.
+
+The patch viewer lists path transfers even without a text change. In a transfer with edits it displays the transfer first and counts the file once. Both coordinates in subsequent hunks must move forward or touch the previous boundary. Git's zero-length range refers to the boundary after its start line. The viewer accepts Git's suppressed empty context and concatenated format-patch mail. Attachments show which parts of mail are visible and where errors are reported.
+
+The coverage dashboard combines independent producers. Named TN jobs publish complete snapshots per normalized source: a retry supersedes that job's previous source record, including observations now absent. Other jobs and anonymous sections contribute independently. The record count covers contributing sections. Windows drive letters use upper case; drive and UNC roots survive parent traversal. Elsewhere filenames retain case. Compiler exporters include optional function end lines in FN, and grouped FNL/FNA records. The sample exports illustrate the identity and lifetime of each kind of function observation.
+
+The test inspector also imports multiplexed runs. A tagged run uses "[lane] " before every physical line. The inspector enumerates lanes by first appearance, then each lane's normal result order. It shows the lane on each tagged row and uses physical input positions in errors (global EOF for a lane ending early). Parent names and scope components have the same display escaping as leaf labels. Buffered and streamed subtests use suite-local numbering and emit children before the closing result. Diagnostic attachments are opaque.
+
+Add two new passing tests in each repaired subsystem. The release gate recognizes diff_archive_regression and diff_boundary_regression, lcov_archive_regression and lcov_boundary_regression, tap_archive_regression and tap_boundary_regression. Use a new example to demonstrate an archive incident and a neighboring boundary condition for each pair.
